{"units": [{"id": "mvp-comment-208-7-mentioned1", "translation": "unwept"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-208-7-mentioned2", "translation": "unlamented"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-208-7-mentioned3", "translation": "unseen"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-208-7-mentioned4", "translation": "he went unseen, unheard of"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-208-7-mentioned5", "translation": "alpha privative"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-208-7-mentioned6", "translation": "Polites"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-208-7-mentioned7", "translation": "Athena"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-208-7-mentioned8", "translation": "army, host"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-208-7-mentioned9", "translation": "king"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-208-7-mentioned10", "translation": "former, earlier"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-208-7-mentioned11", "translation": "later account"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-209-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ 'people' here often: 569, 668, 686, 762, 889; so also Pindar, as Pyth. 2, 87 ⟦2⟧ = ⟦3⟧."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-209-1-mentioned1", "translation": "army, host"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-209-1-mentioned2", "translation": "the violent host"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-209-1-mentioned3", "translation": "people"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-209-2-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ (or perhaps ⟦2⟧, as the manuscript, cf. ⟦3⟧ ⟦4⟧; but ⟦5⟧ ⟦6⟧, ⟦7⟧ ⟦8⟧) is as little an aorist as ⟦9⟧ 438; the middle voice is justified by the fact that the herald, as an official, belongs to the council. The model for the passage is clearly Homer Σ 503 (court scene): ⟦10⟧ (cf. also B 96 ff.)."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-209-2-mentioned1", "translation": "he was being restrained"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-209-2-mentioned2", "translation": "you were being restrained"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-209-2-mentioned3", "translation": "unrestrained"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-209-2-mentioned4", "translation": "to restrain"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-209-2-mentioned5", "translation": "he was restrained"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-209-2-mentioned6", "translation": "you were defending"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-209-2-mentioned7", "translation": "and the heralds were restraining the people"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-1-comment1", "translation": "In V. 567 there is an old variant ⟦1⟧ for ⟦2⟧, and the ⟦3⟧' ⟦4⟧ can be compared with ⟦5⟧ 412, ⟦6⟧ ⟦7⟧. 474, since this also stands in the second clause; thus the scholiast is right: ⟦8⟧. At the beginning the verse is mutilated: perhaps 〈⟦9⟧〉.. The interpreters seem to go far astray who seek in ⟦10⟧ a form of ⟦11⟧, while ⟦12⟧ just as little as ⟦13⟧. 181 needs an addition, and the concept 'heaven' has nothing to do here at all. The anachronism in ⟦14⟧ is noted by the scholia; cf. ⟦15⟧ (⟦16⟧, Paley). We do not know that the trumpet had a place in the Athenian judicial system; the ⟦17⟧ Dem. 16, 169 is related to the generals. On 568 cf. ⟦18⟧ ⟦19⟧, on 569 ⟦20⟧ ⟦21⟧ (= ⟦22⟧a Ddf., 623 N.)."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-1-mentioned1", "translation": "or then"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-1-mentioned2", "translation": "or then"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-1-mentioned3", "translation": "the"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-1-mentioned4", "translation": "then"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-1-mentioned5", "translation": "neither then"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-1-mentioned6", "translation": "nor then"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-1-mentioned7", "translation": "as if the herald alone were not sufficient"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-1-mentioned8", "translation": "the rest"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-1-mentioned9", "translation": "then"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-1-mentioned10", "translation": "heaven"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-1-mentioned11", "translation": "piercing"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-1-mentioned12", "translation": "Tyrrhenian trumpet"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-1-mentioned13", "translation": "trumpeter"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-1-mentioned14", "translation": "filled with nostril-proud blasts"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-1-mentioned15", "translation": "over-loud shout"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-2-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ is, as at 683, 687, not the space, but the assembly itself (cf. ⟦2⟧), therefore ⟦3⟧; ⟦4⟧ and ⟦5⟧ (⟦6⟧ Andok. 1, 112) are standard for the becoming full of an assembly or manning (⟦7⟧ ⟦8⟧ Arist. Eccl. 89. V. 571"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-2-mentioned1", "translation": "council chamber"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-2-mentioned2", "translation": "court"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-2-mentioned3", "translation": "the council of the Areopagus"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-2-mentioned4", "translation": "to be filled"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-2-mentioned5", "translation": "full"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-2-mentioned6", "translation": "the council, when it was full"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-2-quote1", "translation": "), when the assembly was being filled"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-3-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ = ⟦2⟧ Schol. (⟦3⟧ ⟦4⟧ . . ⟦5⟧)."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-3-mentioned1", "translation": "it helps"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-3-mentioned2", "translation": "it benefits"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-3-mentioned3", "translation": "the yoke helps"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-210-3-quote1", "translation": "to bear lightly"}]}